  "published": "2026-11-17T13:45:21.383Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ADDED\n- `ProductDto.FreeTrialPeriod` is the free trial that a purchase of the product starts for the current user (`Value=2, Unit=Week` for two weeks), or `null` when the product has none or the user can no longer get it. A paywall can now promise a trial only to someone who will get it.\n  - Android: the free phase of the product's default subscription option, the one a purchase of the package uses. Google Play leaves out offers the user is not eligible for; an offer with \"Developer determined\" eligibility is always listed.\n  - iOS and Mac Catalyst: the introductory offer when it is a free trial, kept only when RevenueCat reports the user as `Eligible`. `GetOfferings()` checks this when it fetches the offerings; `Unknown`, `Ineligible` or a failed check give `null`.\n\nNOTE\n- Nothing else in `IRevenueCatBilling` or its DTOs changed, and the bindings are the same as in 10.1.0.",
